From cfdab332a125e894dab7060c091097ad64fde243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:56:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] drm/spacemit: add K1 MIPI DSI host driver for commands

Add a MIPI DSI host for the SpacemiT K1 that can send and receive
commands. The link is brought up on the first transfer, at a fixed
1 Gbps per lane, and reset after a failed transfer. There is no video
mode and no DRM bridge yet.

Packet header ECC and payload CRC are computed in software, as the
vendor driver does. Unlike that driver, report failed and unrecognized
reads as errors.

Register layout and sequences come from the SpacemiT vendor kernel.

On hardware, a low-power write completes. Reads do not yet.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
